---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { nom, nif, adreca, email, dataRevisio } from '../../../data/empresa';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
  <style is:global>
    .doc-card {
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
      backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
      padding: 2.5rem;
      border-radius: 16px;
      box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
      color: #1a1a1a;
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
    }
    .doc-card h1 {
      color: #1a1a1a;
      border-bottom: 2px solid #e0e0e0;
      padding-bottom: 0.75rem;
      font-size: 2rem;
    }
    .doc-card h2 {
      color: #2c3e50;
      margin-top: 1.8rem;
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }
    .doc-card p, .doc-card li {
      color: #1a1a1a;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .doc-card a {
      color: #1a73e8;
      text-decoration: underline;
    }
    .doc-card .highlight {
      background-color: #f5f5f5;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      border-left: 6px solid #e74c3c;
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
      border-radius: 4px;
    }
    .doc-card .footer {
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: #555;
      border-top: 1px solid #ddd;
      padding-top: 1rem;
    }
    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .doc-card { padding: 1.5rem; }
    }
  </style>

  <div class="doc-card">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {dataRevisio}</p>

    <p>This Privacy Policy explains how {nom} (hereinafter, "the controller") processes the personal data of users of the "Supporters App" mobile application.</p>

    <div class="highlight">
      <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Controller:</strong> {nom}</li>
        <li><strong>Tax ID (NIF):</strong> {nif}</li>
        <li><strong>Address:</strong> {adreca}</li>
        <li><strong>Contact email (ARCO rights):</strong> <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>2. Data we collect</h2>
    <p>We collect the following personal data:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Alias:</strong> A username freely chosen by the user.</li>
      <li><strong>Internal identifier:</strong> A random code generated by the system to uniquely identify the user.</li>
      <li><strong>Geolocation data:</strong> GPS coordinates of the user (only when using the stadium attendance verification feature).</li>
      <li><strong>Usage data:</strong> Anonymous browsing and interaction statistics (via Firebase Analytics).</li>
      <li><strong>Notification token:</strong> Identifier for sending push notifications (FCM).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Purposes of processing</h2>
    <p>The collected data is processed for the following purposes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Managing user registration and identification within the application.</li>
      <li>Verifying attendance at sporting events by comparing the user's location with stadium coordinates (using a geospatial calculation service).</li>
      <li>Sending push notifications related to the event (reminders, schedule changes, etc.).</li>
      <li>Analyzing application usage to improve user experience.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Legal basis</h2>
    <p>The legal basis for data processing is the user's <strong>explicit consent</strong> (Article 6.1.a of the GDPR), which is given at the time of registration and acceptance of this policy.</p>
    <p>For geolocation, additional and specific consent is requested before activating the feature.</p>

    <h2>5. Data processors (providers)</h2>
    <p>The controller uses the services of the following companies for data processing:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google LLC (Firebase):</strong> Authentication, Firestore database, Remote Config, FCM (notifications), and Analytics. Information at: <a href="https://firebase.google.com/privacy" target="_blank">https://firebase.google.com/privacy</a></li>
      <li><strong>MongoDB, Inc. (Atlas):</strong> Geospatial database for location verification. Information at: <a href="https://www.mongodb.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank">https://www.mongodb.com/legal/privacy-policy</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
    <p>Data stored in Firebase is primarily located on servers within the European Union. However, Google LLC is a company based in the United States, so there is an international data transfer.</p>
    <p>This transfer is covered by the <strong>Standard Contractual Clauses (SCC)</strong> approved by the European Commission, which ensure an adequate level of protection. Users may request further information about these safeguards at the provided email address.</p>

    <h2>7. Data retention</h2>
    <p>Data will be retained as long as the user maintains an active account. After <strong>2 years</strong> of inactivity, the controller may proceed to delete personal data, unless the user requests deletion earlier.</p>

    <h2>8. User rights</h2>
    <p>The user has the right to exercise the following rights at any time by sending a written request to {email}:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access:</strong> Know what data we hold about you.</li>
      <li><strong>Rectification:</strong> Modify inaccurate data.</li>
      <li><strong>Erasure (right to be forgotten):</strong> Delete your data.</li>
      <li><strong>Restriction of processing:</strong> Restrict the use of your data.</li>
      <li><strong>Objection:</strong> Object to processing for specific purposes.</li>
      <li><strong>Portability:</strong> Receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD) if you believe we have not processed your data correctly.</p>

    <div class="footer">
      <p>© {dataRevisio} - {nom}. All rights reserved.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>